"""Knowledge base for the chat assistant (docs/chatbot_rag_finetune.md, steps 1-2).

Two corpora, always labelled, never mixed up:
  * ledger    - facts generated BY CODE from data/processed/app_data.json (every number comes from the pipeline)
  * reference - methodology documents in data/raw/external/reference (GHG Protocol Scope 2, Cloud Carbon Footprint,
                FOCUS, Ember grid data). Explains concepts; never a source of company figures.

Golden rules enforced here:
  * free-text fields of the data (Notes, Remark, description, line_item_description) are never indexed; the four
    planted instructions appear only as QUARANTINED quotes
  * reference chunks are scanned with the same injection patterns and dropped if they match
  * verify_numbers(): every figure in an answer must appear in the retrieved facts (or the question)

Retrieval = exact-ID match + BM25 + dense embeddings (MiniLM), fused by reciprocal rank. Dense vectors are a numpy
matrix (no vector database). Without the optional `finetune` group the index still works with BM25 alone.
"""
